{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2184","id":5261913072,"node_id":"PR_kwDORcHGMc8AAAABOaJr8A","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2184","diff_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2184.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2184.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2184","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2184/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2184/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2184/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/statuses/1c5ca4bb36c0b632c93d8e8b6f2d066c85cd1519","number":2184,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Refs KS-1959: the vc-issuer database probe reads a thrown value's message inside a guard, so a revoked Proxy or a throwing message getter no longer makes the probe reject","user":{"login":"kksecura","id":258699643,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2txew","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258699643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura","html_url":"https://github.com/kksecura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Refs KS-1959: the vc-issuer database probe reads a thrown value's message inside a guard, so a revoked Proxy or a throwing message getter no longer makes the probe reject\n\n**TIER 2 (the commission's tier): PRODUCT BYTES CHANGE, one product file, `Blockchain/Dev/services/vc-issuer/src/db.ts` (+8 -1), and one new test file (+117 -0). The gate may raise the tier.** Merge to develop only.\n\nLinear: https://linear.app/secuura/issue/KS-1959\n\n## Summary\n\n- **What the ticket records.** Finding G152-F4 on KS-1959: a thrown value whose read throws (a revoked Proxy, an Error whose `message` getter throws) makes an unguarded `err?.message` in a catch throw inside the catch. The ticket names `db.ts` `probeDb` among the places that still read the value unguarded. This PR is that one site.\n- **What changes.** The catch of `probeDb` returned `{ ok: false, error: err?.message }`. It now reads the message inside its own `try`: an undefined or null message stays undefined, anything else goes through `String()`, and a read that throws becomes the constant `'unreadable thrown value'`. Eight lines are added and one replaced. A plain thrown string still has no message (the logged `error` stays undefined, as before).\n- **Why it matters here (measured through `initDb`).** With the product at develop, a probe failure that is a revoked Proxy or an Error whose message getter throws makes `probeDb` reject, and `initDb` rejects with it instead of resolving `false` and arming the background retry. An Error whose message is a Symbol reaches the `Database unavailable` log line as the raw Symbol, not text. With the patch all three resolve `false`, and the log line carries text.\n- **What it does NOT do.** It does not touch the `credentialRepo.ts` catches the same finding names (`revoke`, `store`, `getReadableByHash`, `selectList`); another row of the queue owns that file. The retry timer's own call of `probeDb` is covered only by the same function change: its behaviour over time was not run. KS-1959 stays open (`Refs`); its revoke defect was handled by an earlier PR, and closing a ticket is the board seat's act.\n- **Held patch** (a Spark pass, 6,360 B canonical, sha256 prefix `805bbb2a5140bded`): applied strictly at develop `4f85ca04c622`; its changed lines per file equal the applied diff's (cmp rc 0, beside a planted difference that reads rc 1). Nothing in it was changed by Seat R 100th. The coordinating seat held this row for raising.\n\n## Test plan / Test Evidence\n\n**Touched:** two files, `Blockchain/Dev/services/vc-issuer/src/db.ts` (+8 -1) and `Blockchain/Dev/services/vc-issuer/src/__tests__/ks1959-vc-issuer-db-probe-catch-unreadable-throw.test.ts` (new, +117 -0); numstat `8 1` and `117 0`, equal to the held patch's. Base is develop `4f85ca04c622`. The push gate reads origin develop and the move since the base against this row's two paths before anything is sent; the census run before the push read no open pull request on either file (its counts and controls are in the READY mail). The pre-push hook runs the same gate again on the pushed head.\n\n**Ran** (all by Seat R 100th, 2026-11-12, Apple Silicon Mac (arm64), macOS 27.2.1, Node v26.8.1, in tree `s-r100-ks1959`; evidence `evidence/row38/`):\n- **Strict apply:** `git apply --check -p1` rc 0 on develop (a doctored copy read rc 1); the files changed in the tree are the two files in the patch.\n- **Whole vc-issuer suite (vitest, `vitest run`):** on develop 28 files, 842 tests passed, 0 failed (load1 4.85 at its start); with the patch 29 files, 847 tests passed, 0 failed (load1 4.62 at its start). The 5 added tests are the new file's cells.\n- **Red first, then green:** with the product file put back to develop and the new test kept, 3 of the new file's 5 cells fail by assertion (`RED ks1959 R1`, a revoked Proxy; `R2`, an Error whose message getter throws; `R3`, an Error whose message is a Symbol) and the two control cells (`C1`, an ordinary Error; `C2`, a plain string) pass; with the patch re-applied all 5 pass.\n- **Type check with the test files included:** the package's own `tsc` config excludes the tests, so I used a scratch config that extends it (`noEmit`, `types` node): rc 0, 0 error lines, none in the new test (the planted control file reported its one planted error with rc 2, so the check can fail).\n- **eslint** (`npm run lint`, `eslint src`): rc 0; no line names the touched files.\n- **docs-fragments check, in my tree on the applied diff:** rc 0. No fragment is added by this PR.\n\n**NOT run:** a real Postgres or an unreachable database at boot (the cells replace `pg` with a stand-in pool whose query rejects with the armed value); the background retry timer over time; the production logger; the other service suites; the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, k6).\n\n**Migrations + config:** none.\n\n**Pre-push hook:** (quoted from the push of this head by Seat R 100th)\n```\nPREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE — 13/16 legs ran, 3 SKIPPED. Nothing failed.\n  legs 3 4 8 — local stack not up; you can clear this by starting it.\n  This is NOT a pass. Do not quote it as one — say which legs ran.\n```\n- Leg 14, verbatim: `shell suites: 126 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (of 126)`\n\n## Before this deploys\n\n- Nothing deploys from this PR. It reaches develop only; \"deployed\" reads as \"on develop\". The demo is frozen and a vc-issuer deploy is not granted by this PR.\n\n## Notes for the gate\n\n- **Provenance of the raise.** The patch is the Spark operator's pass o140 P1; Seat R 100th applied it strictly, built nothing of its own, and pushed one commit.\n- The test header comment names the ticket's own key, as held.\n- Branch name `feature/ks-1959-vc-issuer-probedb-catch-guards-the-thrown-value-read`: checked, it carries no other ticket's key and no closing word, and it differs from the earlier branch of the merged PR 2005.\n- KS-1959 stays open (`Refs`): closing a ticket is the board seat's act.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-11T15:12:28Z","updated_at":"2026-11-11T15:12:37Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a161b724636c1669609fb7e225d4ab6116bbd940","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Secuura:feature/ks-1959-vc-issuer-probedb-catch-guards-the-thrown-value-read","ref":"feature/ks-1959-vc-issuer-probedb-catch-guards-the-thrown-value-read","repo":{"id":1170327089,"node_id":"R_kgDORcHGMQ","name":"Distributed_Secuura","full_name":"Secuura/Distributed_Secuura","owner":{"login":"Secuura","id":257240886,"node_id":"O_kgDOD1UvNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257240886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":true,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"TypeScript","visibility":"private","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":2,"watchers_count":2,"watchers":2,"open_issues_count":176,"open_issues":176,"size":289280,"default_branch":"main","ha